---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '../../components/layout/Section.astro';
import Container from '../../components/layout/Container.astro';
import LifecycleRibbon from '../../components/marketing/LifecycleRibbon.astro';
import WaitlistForm from '../../components/forms/WaitlistForm.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Smart scheduling"
  description="Runway's offset engine cascades dates downstream as predecessors shift. Every moved activity shows a chevron pointing at the driving predecessor — so the team can see why."
>
  <Section tone="cream">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <header class="head stack-l">
        <p class="eyebrow">Pillar 03 · Smart scheduling</p>
        <h1 class="display step-5">Dates cascade. The team sees why.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          A schedule that doesn't propagate change is just a snapshot. Runway's offset engine
          recalculates every downstream activity when a predecessor moves — and surfaces the
          driving predecessor right on the timeline.
        </p>
      </header>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="ink" pad="tight">
    <Container>
      <header class="rib-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Eight phases. Phase-tagged entities.</p>
        <h2 class="display step-3">The ORAT lifecycle, as a first-class object.</h2>
      </header>
      <LifecycleRibbon />
      <p class="rib-note">Specs, equipment, training, procedures, and trials all carry an ORAT phase tag. Filter to today's phase. Roll up to the program. Pre-seeded from a project-type template on day one.</p>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="paper">
    <Container>
      <div class="row-list">
        <article class="row-item">
          <h3 class="row-title">Offset engine</h3>
          <p>
            Every link can carry an offset in calendar days or working days. When a predecessor's
            date shifts, every downstream activity recalculates. No manual reschedules. No "what did
            this slip impact?" guessing.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="row-item">
          <h3 class="row-title">Driving predecessor</h3>
          <p>
            When an activity has multiple predecessors, the timeline shows a chevron pointing at the
            one currently driving its start date. Click the chevron to navigate straight to it. The
            team understands cascades visually, not from a PDF report.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="row-item">
          <h3 class="row-title">Manual override + audit</h3>
          <p>
            Sometimes the engine is wrong. Set a manual date override and the chevron disappears.
            The override is captured in the history — anyone can see who overrode the cascade and
            why.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="row-item">
          <h3 class="row-title">Phase-aware timeline</h3>
          <p>
            The Program Horizon strip groups activities by ORAT phase: Planning, Design Review,
            Construction, Mobilization, Activation, Live Ops, Closeout. Stakeholders see "where are
            we" at a glance, not "what bar is on what row."
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="row-item">
          <h3 class="row-title">Excel import</h3>
          <p>
            Existing master programs come in as Excel. Runway imports them, maps columns, and
            preserves your IDs so downstream systems keep working. Re-importing updates by ID,
            doesn't duplicate.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="row-item">
          <h3 class="row-title">Zone readiness rollup</h3>
          <p>
            Every readiness activity links to one or more zones. The facility map renders each zone
            with a readiness percentage rolled up from its linked activities. Hover for the
            blockers. Click for the blade.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="cream">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <div class="cta stack-l">
        <p class="eyebrow">See the cascade in action</p>
        <h2 class="display step-3">Schedules that update themselves.</h2>
        <WaitlistForm source="schedule" cta="Request a walkthrough" />
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .step-5 { font-size: var(--step-5); }
  .step-3 { font-size: var(--step-3); }
  .head { max-width: 50rem; }
  .rib-head { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2xs); margin-bottom: var(--space-l); max-width: 50rem; }
  .rib-note { margin-top: var(--space-m); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--step--2); letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: rgba(244, 239, 230, 0.7); }
  .row-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-xl) var(--space-l);
  }
  .row-item { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-s); padding-top: var(--space-l); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .row-title { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--step-1); font-weight: 700; }
  .row-item p { color: var(--ink-soft); }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .row-list { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .cta { text-align: center; align-items: center; }
  .cta :global(.waitlist) { max-width: 28rem; margin-inline: auto; width: 100%; }
</style>
